OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Automations/**`.
That path does NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group. The repo's real,
compiled canonical page home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/` — proven by every DONE
sibling page (ActionBuilderPage, AutomationsListPage, AutomationActivityFeedPage, … all under
Sources/Features/<Domain>). `Sources` is a project.yml source path (createIntermediateGroups),
shared by the iOS + macOS app targets (ADR-002). The page therefore ships at
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/Automations/**` — the faithful equivalent of the prompt's
`Features/Automations`. Strings ship in the platform catalog
`apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This mapping is the only
deviation from the literal prompt path and is recorded here per covenant #9 (identical to the
DONE sibling ActionBuilder's reconciliation).

REUSE / DRY (engineering principles — no duplication of the proven domain core):
The pure, Foundation-only projection layer for this surface already ships, module-public, in the
P4 feature-view (`apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/TriggerConfigurator.{Adapter,Catalog}.swift`):
the discriminated `AutomationTrigger` union, `TriggerKind`, `SignalTrigger`/`SignalValue`/
`SignalOperator`, the `CronExpression.build/parse` schedule helpers + `SimpleSchedule`, the
`TriggerAdapter` weekday-toggle + `signalValue`/`displayValue`/`parseLeadingDouble` coercions, the
`AutomationTrigger.createDefault` seeds, the `Geofence` wire model, the
`VehicleEventCatalog`/`GeofenceEventCatalog`/`SignalOperatorCatalog`/`SignalCatalog`/
`TimezoneCatalog`/`WeekdayCatalog`/`TriggerTypeCatalog` option catalogs, `TriggerOption`, and the
injectable-localizer `TriggerConfiguratorAccessibility` VoiceOver summaries — all take an INJECTED
`localize` closure. This unit REUSES that core (one source of truth, zero type collisions — every
new symbol is `TriggerConfiguratorPage*` / `TriggerConfiguratorGeofence*`) and feeds it a
`Localizable.xcstrings` localizer, then ships a fresh page/model/editors/views/registration that
resolve every string from the platform catalog (the P7 string requirement). No feature-views file
was edited (out of allowed scope).

NAVIGATION (the unit is (unrouted)):
The web `TriggerConfigurator` is a composable SECTION the `/automations` builder page renders inline
— NOT a standalone route. So this unit does NOT take a top-level `AppRoute` (that would hijack a
sibling unit's route). Instead it ships a typed `NavigationDestination` seam —
`TriggerConfiguratorPageLink` + `View.triggerConfiguratorDestination()` +
`TriggerConfiguratorPageRouteRegistration.make(...)` — that any `NavigationStack` adopts to deep-link
the full-screen trigger editor. No edits to the P4 shell (AppShell/AppRoute/TeslaSyncApp) were made —
correct for an unrouted unit (covenant #7).

SCREEN COMPOSITION (faithful to the bare web component):
The web component returns a bare `space-y-4` stack with no panel chrome (the host supplies it) and
switches on `trigger.kind`. As a self-contained P7 screen this page hosts the web source's exported
`TRIGGER_TYPES` picker (reused `TriggerTypeCatalog`) above the per-kind editor inside a `tsGlassPanel`
(the host chrome), so every one of the four editors (schedule / event / geofence / signal) is reachable
and every region the web `switch` renders is reproduced in the same data + grouping + order.

UNITS / LIVE DATA (honest scope):
TriggerConfigurator has NO unit-bearing display values — the signal threshold is a raw user-entered
comparison value (web stores `value_num` verbatim), so no SI conversion is applied at the boundary
(P1/S5 not needed here; nothing is computed/stored non-SI). `useGeofences` (`GET /geofences`) is a
one-shot fetch, NOT a live SSE source, so no SSE subscription / >2-min staleness overlay is modeled
(ADR-013 applies only to live streams) — load()/refresh() mirror the hook's query/refetch.

